window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"{\"title\":\"CAPM Mock Practice Tests\",\"total\":700,\"sections\":[{\"id\":\"fundamentals\",\"title\":\"PM Fundamentals and Core Concepts\",\"kind\":\"Domain Practice\",\"count\":25,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">During product validation, a key stakeholder refused to sign off on the acceptance document, stating that certain functionalities did not meet their expectations. What could the project manager have done to prevent this situation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During product validation, a key stakeholder refused to sign off on the acceptance document, stating that certain functionalities did not meet their expectations. What could the project manager have done to prevent this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sX\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Engage the key stakeholder during the quality control phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Engage the key stakeholder during the quality control phase\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Engage the key stakeholder during the project initiation phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Engage the key stakeholder during the project initiation phase\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Engage the key stakeholder during the planning phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Engage the key stakeholder during the planning phase\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Engage the key stakeholder during all project phases<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Engage the key stakeholder during all project phases\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">Stakeholders need to get involved early on during project planning and sometimes during the project initiation as well. Key stakeholders should also be involved during the quality control phase so that they can assess the project deliverables and recommend any changes before the official acceptance. Since the concerned key stakeholder is responsible for signing off the acceptance document, their power is considered high. Therefore, stakeholders who are identified to have high power using the power/interest grid should be managed closely and kept satisfied throughout the whole project.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Stakeholders need to get involved early on during project planning and sometimes during the project initiation as well. Key stakeholders should also be involved during the quality control phase so that they can assess the project deliverables and recommend any changes before the official acceptance. Since the concerned key stakeholder is responsible for signing off the acceptance document, their power is considered high. Therefore, stakeholders who are identified to have high power using the power/interest grid should be managed closely and kept satisfied throughout the whole project.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which of the following documents does the project manager need to develop the project charter? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following documents does the project manager need to develop the project charter? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Strategic plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Strategic plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business case<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Business case\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Agreements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Agreements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project Management Plan\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Cost Management Plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Cost Management Plan\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">To develop the Project Charter, the project manager needs business documents such as the project’s business case, benefits/strategic plan, and agreements. The Project Management Plan and the Cost Management Plan are developed once the project charter is signed.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C To develop the Project Charter, the project manager needs business documents such as the project’s business case, benefits/strategic plan, and agreements. The Project Management Plan and the Cost Management Plan are developed once the project charter is signed.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":3,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">A project manager is leading a project that consists of four phases. Which meeting should the project manager hold at each phase to ensure the stakeholders’ continuous commitment? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project that consists of four phases. Which meeting should the project manager hold at each phase to ensure the stakeholders’ continuous commitment?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kickoff meeting <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Kickoff meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Retrospective meeting <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Retrospective meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Risk review meeting <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Risk review meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Stage gate meeting <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stage gate meeting\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = D<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Stage-gate or phase review meetings represent an opportunity for project stakeholders to review project progress along with planned future actions. In these meetings, project stakeholders can assess whether or not the project is on track to meet the organization’s expectations (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 42). The project manager should schedule gate meetings at key milestones throughout the project to not only ensure it is on track but also demonstrate to the project stakeholders that the project is staying on course. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Stage-gate or phase review meetings represent an opportunity for project stakeholders to review project progress along with planned future actions. In these meetings, project stakeholders can assess whether or not the project is on track to meet the organization’s expectations (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 42). The project manager should schedule gate meetings at key milestones throughout the project to not only ensure it is on track but also demonstrate to the project stakeholders that the project is staying on course.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":4,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">While overseeing the execution of an industrial project, a project manager observes that two stakeholders are frequently in disagreement, potentially affecting the project negatively. Which of the following options should be used to record and track this type of situation? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"While overseeing the execution of an industrial project, a project manager observes that two stakeholders are frequently in disagreement, potentially affecting the project negatively. Which of the following options should be used to record and track this type of situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Dispute log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Dispute log\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Problem log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Problem log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Change log\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue log <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Issue log\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>= D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The issue log, also called an issue register, is a project document that records and tracks all issues that have a negative impact on the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 185). Once created, it’ll be the project manager’s tool to monitor and communicate all that is going on in the project. Such issues may involve resources leaving the project, conflicting teams, or even individuals with low morale. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Options A &amp; B:<\\/span> Problem log and dispute log are both made-up terms. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A change log is used to document all change requests. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"= D The issue log, also called an issue register, is a project document that records and tracks all issues that have a negative impact on the project (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 185). Once created, it’ll be the project manager’s tool to monitor and communicate all that is going on in the project. Such issues may involve resources leaving the project, conflicting teams, or even individuals with low morale. Options A & B: Problem log and dispute log are both made-up terms. Option C: A change log is used to document all change requests.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":5,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Activities that involve ongoing, routine tasks designed to maintain and support the organization's infrastructure and processes are most likely referred to as ________.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Activities that involve ongoing, routine tasks designed to maintain and support the organization's infrastructure and processes are most likely referred to as ________.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Operations<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Operations\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>A project<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"A project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>A program<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"A program\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\" id=\\\"page_4\\\"><p><span>A portfolio<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"A portfolio\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Operations involve routine, ongoing activities that maintain and support the day-to-day functioning of an organization’s infrastructure and processes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A project is a temporary endeavor undertaken to create a unique product, service, or result. Projects have specific start and end dates and are aimed at achieving a particular goal.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A program is a group of related projects managed in a coordinated way to obtain benefits and control not available from managing them individually. Programs are broader in scope and often focus on achieving long-term objectives<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A portfolio is a collection of projects, programs, subsidiary portfolios, and operations managed together to achieve strategic business objectives.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Operations involve routine, ongoing activities that maintain and support the day-to-day functioning of an organization’s infrastructure and processes. Option B: A project is a temporary endeavor undertaken to create a unique product, service, or result. Projects have specific start and end dates and are aimed at achieving a particular goal. Option C: A program is a group of related projects managed in a coordinated way to obtain benefits and control not available from managing them individually. Programs are broader in scope and often focus on achieving long-term objectives . Option D: A portfolio is a collection of projects, programs, subsidiary portfolios, and operations managed together to achieve strategic business objectives.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project team is reluctant to begin work on a project because key stakeholders may request proper authorization and clearly defined objectives before proceeding. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team is reluctant to begin work on a project because key stakeholders may request proper authorization and clearly defined objectives before proceeding. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cancel the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Cancel the project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start working on the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Start working on the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop the project charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop the project charter\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start working on the project while adding the associated risk to the risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Start working on the project while adding the associated risk to the risk register\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project charter is an official document created by the project initiator or sponsor that formally authorizes the project’s initiation. It grants the project manager the authority to allocate organizational resources and undertake project activities.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> While identifying risks and updating the risk register is important, the project cannot start without getting authorized.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A project charter is an official document created by the project initiator or sponsor that formally authorizes the project’s initiation. It grants the project manager the authority to allocate organizational resources and undertake project activities. Option D: While identifying risks and updating the risk register is important, the project cannot start without getting authorized.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">Upon delivering a rebranding project, the sponsor, as well as other key stakeholders, are hesitant to accept deliverables and close the project. What should the project manager do? (Select three) <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Upon delivering a rebranding project, the sponsor, as well as other key stakeholders, are hesitant to accept deliverables and close the project. What should the project manager do? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and resolve pending issues. Then, be firm on formal closure. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Identify and resolve pending issues. Then, be firm on formal closure.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Formally close the project. Stakeholders will get well-acquainted with the new brand by that time. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Formally close the project. Stakeholders will get well-acquainted with the new brand by that time.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Identify and openly discuss the reasons for reluctance. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Identify and openly discuss the reasons for reluctance.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Invite earnest feedback from all parties and try to identify any misunderstandings. <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Invite earnest feedback from all parties and try to identify any misunderstandings.\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Negotiate a new project scope <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Negotiate a new project scope\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A, C, D<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The project manager should not close the project when key stakeholders are not satisfied. They should try to discuss, identify, and resolve any issues or misunderstandings first. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D The project manager should not close the project when key stakeholders are not satisfied. They should try to discuss, identify, and resolve any issues or misunderstandings first.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">All of the following statements are true, except:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"All of the following statements are true, except:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A project can involve multiple stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A project can involve multiple stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A program is a large project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A program is a large project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio management aligns with organizational strategy<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Portfolio management aligns with organizational strategy\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Several projects can be aligned under a single program<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Several projects can be aligned under a single program\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Programs are not big projects. While a program mainly focuses on maximizing the organization's profits, project management targets the creation of deliverables that meet and satisfy stakeholder needs.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Programs are not big projects. While a program mainly focuses on maximizing the organization's profits, project management targets the creation of deliverables that meet and satisfy stakeholder needs.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which interpersonal skills does a project manager use frequently in a project? (Select three answers)<br/><\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which interpersonal skills does a project manager use frequently in a project? (Select three answers)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Emotional intelligence<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Emotional intelligence\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Negotiation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Negotiation\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Decision making<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Decision making\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conflict management<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Conflict management\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Networking<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Networking\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Interpersonal skills that are used frequently in projects include emotional intelligence, decision making, and conflict resolution. These are the skills used to establish and maintain relationships with others (PMBOK 7th edition, page 24). Emotional intelligence is the ability to recognize, understand, manage, and effectively be aware of the emotions of oneself and others. Throughout the project, daily decisions are made, therefore a project manager should exhibit the right choice of decision-making technique and approach. Moreover, Conflict management is crucial as it’s the ability to handle and resolve conflicts within a project team.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D Interpersonal skills that are used frequently in projects include emotional intelligence, decision making, and conflict resolution. These are the skills used to establish and maintain relationships with others (PMBOK 7th edition, page 24). Emotional intelligence is the ability to recognize, understand, manage, and effectively be aware of the emotions of oneself and others. Throughout the project, daily decisions are made, therefore a project manager should exhibit the right choice of decision-making technique and approach. Moreover, Conflict management is crucial as it’s the ability to handle and resolve conflicts within a project team.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project manager is working on a contract. After completing the contract and closing the project, she finds herself without work. What type of organizational structure does the project manager work in?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is working on a contract. After completing the contract and closing the project, she finds herself without work. What type of organizational structure does the project manager work in?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Strong matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Strong matrix\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Projectized<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Projectized\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Functional<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Functional\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Weak matri<span><\\/span>x<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Weak matri x\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A Project-oriented organization, or a projectized organization, is one in which a considerable part of its processes and activities take place in the form of projects. There is no defined hierarchy; resources are brought together specifically for a project. Once the project is finished, they’re either moved to a new project or released.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A Project-oriented organization, or a projectized organization, is one in which a considerable part of its processes and activities take place in the form of projects. There is no defined hierarchy; resources are brought together specifically for a project. Once the project is finished, they’re either moved to a new project or released.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">You are managing six projects at the same time within the company. Two projects are of a similar type, while the other four are completely different. You work as a ______________. <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"You are managing six projects at the same time within the company. Two projects are of a similar type, while the other four are completely different. You work as a ______________.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Portfolio manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Program manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Project manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program coordinator<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Program coordinator\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">In portfolio management, a group of related or non-related programs and projects are managed in coordination (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 244). Portfolio management is intended to reduce the gap between strategy and implementation by aligning projects to attain business objectives.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A In portfolio management, a group of related or non-related programs and projects are managed in coordination (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 244). Portfolio management is intended to reduce the gap between strategy and implementation by aligning projects to attain business objectives.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">During the kick-off meeting of their first project, the project manager presents the project plan to stakeholders. As they go through the details, a stakeholder expressed frustration with the plan's inaccuracies in reflecting their expectations. What is the most likely reason behind the project manager’s inaccurate description of stakeholder requirements?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the kick-off meeting of their first project, the project manager presents the project plan to stakeholders. As they go through the details, a stakeholder expressed frustration with the plan's inaccuracies in reflecting their expectations. What is the most likely reason behind the project manager’s inaccurate description of stakeholder requirements?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager did not use the project scope as a guide when creating the project plan.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project manager did not use the project scope as a guide when creating the project plan.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager only presented the first draft of the project plan, so it can always be improved.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project manager only presented the first draft of the project plan, so it can always be improved.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager did not engage the project stakeholders sufficiently to accurately capture their requirements.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project manager did not engage the project stakeholders sufficiently to accurately capture their requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project manager did not explain the plan well enough. A better presentation would have prevented this misunderstanding.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project manager did not explain the plan well enough. A better presentation would have prevented this misunderstanding.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project manager most likely failed to engage stakeholders adequately, leading to poorly defined requirements and dissatisfaction. Effective stakeholder engagement is needed for identifying needs and aligning the project scope with expectations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Since the project plan is based on the scope, if the scope is not collaboratively defined, the plan will most likely fail to meet stakeholders’ expectations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Given that the plan is being presented at a kick-off meeting, this suggests a predictive project, where a final or well-developed plan is typically presented for stakeholder approval, rather than a draft.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The stakeholders' dissatisfaction is with the plan's content, not its presentation.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project manager most likely failed to engage stakeholders adequately, leading to poorly defined requirements and dissatisfaction. Effective stakeholder engagement is needed for identifying needs and aligning the project scope with expectations. Option A: Since the project plan is based on the scope, if the scope is not collaboratively defined, the plan will most likely fail to meet stakeholders’ expectations. Option B: Given that the plan is being presented at a kick-off meeting, this suggests a predictive project, where a final or well-developed plan is typically presented for stakeholder approval, rather than a draft. Option D: The stakeholders' dissatisfaction is with the plan's content, not its presentation.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project involves numerous stakeholders due to its multiple phases and various tasks to execute. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project involves numerous stakeholders due to its multiple phases and various tasks to execute. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Disregard low-power stakeholders<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Disregard low-power stakeholders\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Only engage stakeholders with high interest in the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Only engage stakeholders with high interest in the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Analyze all stakeholders in order to prioritize engagement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Analyze all stakeholders in order to prioritize engagement\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Report the issue to the project sponsor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Report the issue to the project sponsor\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">You should identify all project stakeholders, regardless of their number, and then analyze each one of them in order to prioritize the engagement (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 12).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> As a project manager, you cannot leave out or disregard any stakeholders.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Ignoring any of the project stakeholders can be very costly and can dramatically impact the project.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Stakeholder engagement falls under the project manager’s responsibilities, and should not be delegated to the sponsor.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C You should identify all project stakeholders, regardless of their number, and then analyze each one of them in order to prioritize the engagement (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 12). Option A: As a project manager, you cannot leave out or disregard any stakeholders. Option B: Ignoring any of the project stakeholders can be very costly and can dramatically impact the project. Option D: Stakeholder engagement falls under the project manager’s responsibilities, and should not be delegated to the sponsor.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">During the planning phase, the project manager assumed that the composition of the project’s steering committee would remain the same. But, since any change could be very critical to the project, the project manager assigned a team member to monitor potential triggers. Where should the name of the person responsible for monitoring the steering committee be documented?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the planning phase, the project manager assumed that the composition of the project’s steering committee would remain the same. But, since any change could be very critical to the project, the project manager assigned a team member to monitor potential triggers. Where should the name of the person responsible for monitoring the steering committee be documented?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Risk register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Issue log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Change log\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder register\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A risk register contains a list of all identified risks, their description, planned responses, probability, impact, risk owner, etc. (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 185). In the described scenario, the change in the composition of the steering committee is considered a risk and the name of the person responsible for managing it should be noted in the risk register. Once the risk occurs, it becomes an issue.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Since the described situation doesn’t involve any issues yet, the issue log is not the Correct Answer.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The situation doesn’t involve any change requests. Therefore, a change log is not the right option.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The stakeholder register includes information about the project stakeholders and their classification. Unlike the stakeholder engagement plan, the stakeholder register doesn’t contain action items for when, how, and who should monitor and engage stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A risk register contains a list of all identified risks, their description, planned responses, probability, impact, risk owner, etc. (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 185). In the described scenario, the change in the composition of the steering committee is considered a risk and the name of the person responsible for managing it should be noted in the risk register. Once the risk occurs, it becomes an issue. Option B: Since the described situation doesn’t involve any issues yet, the issue log is not the Correct Answer. Option C: The situation doesn’t involve any change requests. Therefore, a change log is not the right option. Option D: The stakeholder register includes information about the project stakeholders and their classification. Unlike the stakeholder engagement plan, the stakeholder register doesn’t contain action items for when, how, and who should monitor and engage stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The project sponsor informed the project manager that if the project costs exceed $350,000 by the end of the year, the project will receive no further funding. This is an example of which of the following<span><\\/span>?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project sponsor informed the project manager that if the project costs exceed $350,000 by the end of the year, the project will receive no further funding. This is an example of which of the following ?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Assumption<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Assumption\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Constraint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Issue\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A constraint is a limiting factor that restricts the options for managing a project, program, portfolio, or process. In this case, the following is a budget constraint that limits the project spending.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> An issue is a present condition or situation that can potentially affect the project's objectives.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A constraint is a limiting factor that restricts the options for managing a project, program, portfolio, or process. In this case, the following is a budget constraint that limits the project spending. Option C: An issue is a present condition or situation that can potentially affect the project's objectives.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">The project team will hold a monthly status review meeting with the product owner to review post-iteration deliverables. What’s the best communication type to use in a status review meeting?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project team will hold a monthly status review meeting with the product owner to review post-iteration deliverables. What’s the best communication type to use in a status review meeting?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Push<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Push\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pull<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Pull\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interactive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Interactive\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Formal<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Formal\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">When an immediate response is required and the information you’re communicating is sensitive and could be misinterpreted, you should use interactive communication. It involves one or more people sharing thoughts and ideas, with participants responding in real-time. Interactive communication can take place through teleconferences or face-to-face contact. When using communication media such as emails, the project manager can’t pick up on stakeholders’ facial expressions and body language.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C When an immediate response is required and the information you’re communicating is sensitive and could be misinterpreted, you should use interactive communication. It involves one or more people sharing thoughts and ideas, with participants responding in real-time. Interactive communication can take place through teleconferences or face-to-face contact. When using communication media such as emails, the project manager can’t pick up on stakeholders’ facial expressions and body language.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>What is considered an enterprise environmental factor?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is considered an enterprise environmental factor?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organization policies<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Organization policies\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational culture<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Organizational culture\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organization’s performance data<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Organization’s performance data\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organization’s lessons learned<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Organization’s lessons learned\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEFs) refer to conditions, not under the control of the project team, that influence, constrain, or direct the project.  These conditions could be internal or external to the organization. Organizational Culture is classified as an internal EEFs (PMI Process Groups, page 38).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A, C, D:<\\/span> The organization's policies, lessons learned, and work performance data are organizational process assets, not Enterprise Environmental Factors.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Enterprise Environmental Factors (EEFs) refer to conditions, not under the control of the project team, that influence, constrain, or direct the project.  These conditions could be internal or external to the organization. Organizational Culture is classified as an internal EEFs (PMI Process Groups, page 38). Options A, C, D: The organization's policies, lessons learned, and work performance data are organizational process assets, not Enterprise Environmental Factors.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">What does this table represent?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"What does this table represent?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>RACI chart<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"RACI chart\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Requirements Traceability Matrix<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Requirements Traceability Matrix\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>Stakeholder engagement assessment matrix<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Stakeholder engagement assessment matrix\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>Mood chart<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Mood chart\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Stakeholder Engagement Assessment Matrix is a matrix that shows stakeholder engagement levels.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Stakeholder Engagement Assessment Matrix is a matrix that shows stakeholder engagement levels.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Place the following estimations in their right position on the graph below:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>High accuracy, High precision<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Low accuracy, Low precision<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Low accuracy, High precision<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s7V\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>High accuracy, Low precision<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\" id=\\\"page_7\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Place the following estimations in their right position on the graph below: ● High accuracy, High precision ● Low accuracy, Low precision ● Low accuracy, High precision ● High accuracy, Low precision\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sBZ-1\\\">Correct Answer:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><p class=\\\"class_s9M-2\\\">Accuracy describes how close a measurement is to an accepted value. Precision describes the statistical variability of produced measurement (it can be far off the accepted value) (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 55)<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer: Accuracy describes how close a measurement is to an accepted value. Precision describes the statistical variability of produced measurement (it can be far off the accepted value) (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 55) .\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A\"],[\"B\",\"B\"],[\"C\",\"C\"],[\"D\",\"D\"]],\"options\":[[\"ha-hp\",\"High accuracy, High precision\"],[\"la-lp\",\"Low accuracy, Low precision\"],[\"la-hp\",\"Low accuracy, High precision\"],[\"ha-lp\",\"High accuracy, Low precision\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"ha-hp\",\"B\":\"ha-lp\",\"C\":\"la-hp\",\"D\":\"la-lp\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Industries, such as infrastructure, aerospace, and automotive, use ________________ for directional alignment and integration of component activities. The success of these initiatives is measured by the realization of intended benefits and the efficiency of delivering those benefits.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Industries, such as infrastructure, aerospace, and automotive, use ________________ for directional alignment and integration of component activities. The success of these initiatives is measured by the realization of intended benefits and the efficiency of delivering those benefits.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Projects<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Projects\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Processes<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Processes\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Programs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Programs\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Products<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Products\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Many industries, such as infrastructure, aerospace, and automotive, use program management guides and frameworks. A program is a group of related projects managed in a coordinated way to obtain benefits and control not available from managing them individually. Programs are broader in scope and often focus on achieving long-term objectives (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 224).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Many industries, such as infrastructure, aerospace, and automotive, use program management guides and frameworks. A program is a group of related projects managed in a coordinated way to obtain benefits and control not available from managing them individually. Programs are broader in scope and often focus on achieving long-term objectives (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 224).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":21,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following best describes the &quot;Project Life Cycle&quot;?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following best describes the \\\"Project Life Cycle\\\"?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A set of planning steps that guide project stakeholders throughout the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. A set of planning steps that guide project stakeholders throughout the project.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A collection of processes used to manage the project's execution and monitoring.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. A collection of processes used to manage the project's execution and monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>A sequence of tasks that the project team performs to deliver outputs.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. A sequence of tasks that the project team performs to deliver outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The series of phases that a project passes through from start to completion.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The series of phases that a project passes through from start to completion.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The phases include initiation, planning, execution, monitoring, and closing, and they guide a project from inception to delivery and closure.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> “A set of planning steps that guide project stakeholders throughout the project” describes project planning processes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> “A collection of processes used to manage the project's execution and monitoring” refers to process groups but does not capture the full scope of the project life cycle.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> “A sequence of tasks that the project team performs to deliver outputs” is more aligned with work breakdown structures or activity sequencing rather than the concept of the project life cycle.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The phases include initiation, planning, execution, monitoring, and closing, and they guide a project from inception to delivery and closure. Option A: “A set of planning steps that guide project stakeholders throughout the project” describes project planning processes. Option B: “A collection of processes used to manage the project's execution and monitoring” refers to process groups but does not capture the full scope of the project life cycle. Option C: “A sequence of tasks that the project team performs to deliver outputs” is more aligned with work breakdown structures or activity sequencing rather than the concept of the project life cycle.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":22,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>Which of the following is NOT considered a characteristic of a high-performing project team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is NOT considered a characteristic of a high-performing project team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptability to shifting project demands and challenges<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Adaptability to shifting project demands and challenges\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Frequent and clear communication among team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Frequent and clear communication among team members\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Strong focus on individual achievements over collective goals<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Strong focus on individual achievements over collective goals\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaboration and mutual trust among team members<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Collaboration and mutual trust among team members\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">High-performing teams prioritize collaboration, shared goals, and collective success rather than individual accomplishments.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C High-performing teams prioritize collaboration, shared goals, and collective success rather than individual accomplishments.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":23,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>How should a project manager promote resilience within the project team?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"How should a project manager promote resilience within the project team?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Avoid high-pressure situations that may challenge the team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Avoid high-pressure situations that may challenge the team\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Encourage the team to learn from failures and adapt to changes quickly<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Encourage the team to learn from failures and adapt to changes quickly\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ensure the project plan does not change once approved<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Ensure the project plan does not change once approved\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Minimize feedback from external stakeholders to avoid disruptions<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Minimize feedback from external stakeholders to avoid disruptions\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A resilient team is one that can adapt and recover from setbacks. Encouraging the team to learn from failures fosters a growth mindset and helps them to handle challenges with flexibility and perseverance.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B A resilient team is one that can adapt and recover from setbacks. Encouraging the team to learn from failures fosters a growth mindset and helps them to handle challenges with flexibility and perseverance.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":24,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A project manager is conducting a stakeholder analysis using the power/interest grid. Place the following actions in the corresponding spaces on the matrix:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Monitor<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Keep Satisfied<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Manage Closely<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s7V\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Keep Informed<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is conducting a stakeholder analysis using the power/interest grid. Place the following actions in the corresponding spaces on the matrix: ● Monitor ● Keep Satisfied ● Manage Closely ● Keep Informed\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><ol class=\\\"class_s7K-1\\\"><li><p>Keep Satisfied: Due to their influence, stakeholders with high power and low interest should be kept satisfied. But, because they don’t have a high interest in your project, they can get bored if you over-communicate with them. <\\/p><\\/li><li><p>Manage Closely: Stakeholders with high power and high interest are the most important to your project, and you should make sure to keep them happy by managing them closely. <\\/p><\\/li><li><p>Monitor: Stakeholders with low power and low interest should be kept informed periodically without overdoing it. <\\/p><\\/li><li><p>Keep Informed: You’ll want to keep stakeholders with low power and high interest informed by checking in with them regularly to make sure they are not experiencing any issues or problems. <\\/p><\\/li><\\/ol><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\">Please note that in the real exam, such a question usually comes in the form of “drag &amp; drop”.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer: Keep Satisfied: Due to their influence, stakeholders with high power and low interest should be kept satisfied. But, because they don’t have a high interest in your project, they can get bored if you over-communicate with them. Manage Closely: Stakeholders with high power and high interest are the most important to your project, and you should make sure to keep them happy by managing them closely. Monitor: Stakeholders with low power and low interest should be kept informed periodically without overdoing it. Keep Informed: You’ll want to keep stakeholders with low power and high interest informed by checking in with them regularly to make sure they are not experiencing any issues or problems. Please note that in the real exam, such a question usually comes in the form of “drag & drop”.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A\"],[\"B\",\"B\"],[\"C\",\"C\"],[\"D\",\"D\"]],\"options\":[[\"monitor\",\"Monitor\"],[\"keep-satisfied\",\"Keep Satisfied\"],[\"manage-closely\",\"Manage Closely\"],[\"keep-informed\",\"Keep Informed\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"keep-satisfied\",\"B\":\"manage-closely\",\"C\":\"monitor\",\"D\":\"keep-informed\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":25,\"stemHtml\":\"<p>The person who is motivating and influencing the project team toward a common goal is best defined as a(n) ________ .<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The person who is motivating and influencing the project team toward a common goal is best defined as a(n) ________ .\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Coordinator<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Coordinator\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Supervisor<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Supervisor\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Leader<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Leader\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p>Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A leader's primary role involves inspiring, motivating, and influencing team members to work towards a shared vision or common goal. Leadership focuses on people and their development, aiming to foster collaboration, build trust, and guide the team toward successful outcomes.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A leader's primary role involves inspiring, motivating, and influencing team members to work towards a shared vision or common goal. Leadership focuses on people and their development, aiming to foster collaboration, build trust, and guide the team toward successful outcomes.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null}]},{\"id\":\"predictive\",\"title\":\"Predictive, Plan-based Methodologies\",\"kind\":\"Domain Practice\",\"count\":25,\"questions\":[{\"n\":1,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">When the dimensions of the dug canals for the new dam project were compared to the plan, a significant variance was discovered. As a result, the project manager had to hold a meeting with the team to decide on the next steps. To which of the following process groups does the project manager’s activity belong?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When the dimensions of the dug canals for the new dam project were compared to the plan, a significant variance was discovered. As a result, the project manager had to hold a meeting with the team to decide on the next steps. To which of the following process groups does the project manager’s activity belong?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Executing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Executing\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Closing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Closing\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Monitoring and Controlling<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Monitoring and Controlling\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inspecting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Inspecting\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Reviewing the project performance in comparison to plans is part of the monitoring and controlling process group. These processes are meant for tracking, adjusting, and reporting on the project performance, as well as implementing corrective actions when needed to ensure the project is on track, budget and time-wise. Inspecting is not a process group, it’s rather a risk identification activity.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Reviewing the project performance in comparison to plans is part of the monitoring and controlling process group. These processes are meant for tracking, adjusting, and reporting on the project performance, as well as implementing corrective actions when needed to ensure the project is on track, budget and time-wise. Inspecting is not a process group, it’s rather a risk identification activity.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":2,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">After creating the network diagram, the project manager identified three critical paths. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"After creating the network diagram, the project manager identified three critical paths. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Approve the network diagram and monitor all three critical paths closely.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Approve the network diagram and monitor all three critical paths closely.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Approve the network diagram and focus on monitoring the longest path.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Approve the network diagram and focus on monitoring the longest path.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review the network diagram since it should only have one critical path.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Review the network diagram since it should only have one critical path.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review the network diagram since it shouldn’t have more than two critical paths.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Review the network diagram since it shouldn’t have more than two critical paths.\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project manager should approve the network diagram and closely monitor all three critical paths. Theoretically, there is no limit on how many critical paths a network diagra";
